{"qid": "c01", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The transmitter feeding FIC-10-1 is FT-10-1, which is covered by the Rosemount 3051 datasheet (00813-0100-4001). Per that datasheet, when self-diagnostics detect a sensor or microprocessor failure, the analog signal is driven either high or low to alert the user; the default is a high alarm (≥ 21.75 mA, or ≥ 22.5 mA in the NAMUR-compliant configuration, versus ≤ 3.75 mA / ≤ 3.6 mA for a low alarm). The alarm direction is user-selectable with a jumper/switch on the transmitter, and the alarm levels can be ordered/configured via the alarm-levels option codes: C4 (NAMUR alarm high), CN (NAMUR alarm low), CR/CS (custom high/low alarm and saturation levels, requiring option code C1), or CT (Rosemount standard low alarm). Note the datasheet states the alarm levels option is only available with the HART 4–20 mA output (code A).", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [88, 109, 15, 46, 35, 86, 83, 26, 74, 57, 62, 42]}], "latency_s": 2.7327697000000626, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 201278, "completion_tokens": 392, "cost_usd": 0.00664303, "spent_usd": 0.00664303, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 88, "score": 0.5972}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 109, "score": 0.5398}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 15, "score": 0.5389}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 46, "score": 0.528}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 35, "score": 0.5277}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 86, "score": 0.5255}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 83, "score": 