{"qid": "c04", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The valve operated by FIC-11-1 is FV-11-1, a globe valve covered by the Fisher ET valve datasheet (fisher-et-d100022x012). Its Table 14 lists the available seal materials and their temperature capabilities: a PTFE disk seat is rated -73 to 204°C (-100 to 400°F); the backup ring is available in fluorocarbon (-18 to 204°C / 0 to 400°F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232°C / -40 to 450°F), or nitrile (-40 to 71°C / -40 to 160°F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82°C / -40 to 180°F for other compatible fluids); the seal ring is carbon-filled PTFE rated -73 to 232°C (-100 to 450°F); the spring-loaded valve plug seal uses a PTFE seal ring with an N10276 spring rated -73 to 232°C (-100 to 450°F); and for applications with PEEK anti-extrusion rings, a PTFE/graphite seal ring with an R30003 spring is rated -73 to 316°C (-100 to 600°F). The datasheet also notes that temperatures above 232°C / 450°F require PEEK anti-extrusion rings and a spring-loaded seal ring, extending use to 316°C / 600°F for non-oxidizing service and 260°C / 500°F for oxidizing service.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [22, 21, 2, 12, 20, 5, 11, 4, 8]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [7]}, {"document_id": "swagelok-ms-01-176", "pages": [15, 14]}], "latency_s": 3.004796199966222, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 205903, "completion_tokens": 504, "cost_usd": 0.00716189, "spent_usd": 0.00716189, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 0, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 22, "score": 0.7348}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 21, "score": 0.7306}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 7, "score": 0.7229}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 2, "score": 0.7214}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 12, "score": 0.7094}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 20, "score": 0.7038}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 5, "score": 0.6971}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 11, "score": 0.6869}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 4, "score": 0.6829}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 8, "score": 0.6801}, {"document_id": "swagelok-ms-01-176", "page": 15, "score": 0.677}, {"document_id": "swagelok-ms-01-176", "page": 14, "score": 0.6767}], "prompt_chars": 510964, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The valve operated by FIC-11-1 is FV-11-1, a globe valve covered by the Fisher ET valve datasheet (fisher-et-d100022x012). Its Table 14 lists the available seal materials and their temperature capabilities: a PTFE disk seat is rated -73 to 204°C (-100 to 400°F); the backup ring is available in fluorocarbon (-18 to 204°C / 0 to 400°F), ethylene-propylene (-40 to 232°C / -40 to 450°F), or nitrile (-40 to 71°C / -40 to 160°F for air and hydrocarbons, -40 to 82°C / -40 to 180°F for other compatible fluids); the seal ring is carbon-filled PTFE rated -73 to 232°C (-100 to 450°F); the spring-loaded valve plug seal uses a PTFE seal ring with an N10276 spring rated -73 to 232°C (-100 to 450°F); and for applications with PEEK anti-extrusion rings, a PTFE/graphite seal ring with an R30003 spring is rated -73 to 316°C (-100 to 600°F). The datasheet also notes that temperatures above 232°C / 450°F require PEEK anti-extrusion rings and a spring-loaded seal ring, extending use to 316°C / 600°F for non-oxidizing service and 260°C / 500°F for oxidizing service.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
